3.15.m:
Then, on that portion of the auspicious pedestal, one should place a lotus
having eight auspicious petals; in its middle, on the pericarp, the sun.
There on the petals, one should arrange the guardians of the directions according to their directions;
beneath the auspicious pedestal one should fashion the earth.
They know the pillar to be the atmosphere, and the upper part beyond that;
all the foremost gods are present there.
The sky, consisting of all the gods, has been described to you, O strong-armed one;
having worshipped it, one obtains all desires.
This essential nature of the sky has been described by me; by performing worship of the sky, the entire
universe, moving and unmoving, would be worshipped, O sole hero, O foremost of the Yādava lineage!

3.16.m:
Mārkaṇḍeya said:
Nara should be made dark like dūrvā grass and two-armed, O strong-armed one;
Nārāyaṇa has four arms and the radiance of a blue lotus petal.

3.17.m:
