confused with lines and circles, pierced, or combined with vimala mineral. / Vimala should be known as threefold: derived from iron, from bronze, and from gold.
That which is attended by iron vimala causes the destruction of people; / that possessing bronze-like vimala destroys people’s honor;
that combined with golden vimala brings famine as well as drought. / If a circle is seen upon rubbing and cutting,
one should know that [stone] to have a fetus, and should carefully avoid it. / When the womb is resembling madder-red, there is a frog inside;
in a yellowish circle, a monitor lizard; in a black one, he should know there is a snake; / in a tawny one, he should know there is a mouse; in a reddish one, a chameleon;
in a molasses-colored one, a stone; in a dove-colored one, a gecko; / water in one looking like the color of a sword; and sand in an ash-colored one.
Hence, if joined with even one of these, it leads to the ruin of the patron. / Thus stones with fetuses should be known through their external marks.
